WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:04.180
If you want to hear about the origin of the
creatures from this movie, stick around to

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:08.750
the end of this video.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:14.340
OK, I don't think they can hear us here...

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.601
I just ran up to the surface to gather as
many things you missed as I could from the

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:18.780
new movie A Quiet Place.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.449
I'm going to try to tell you all them, and
answer some of your questions from the film.

00:00:22.449 --> 00:00:26.580
As someone who has done sound professionally,
it should be a lot of fun talking about some

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.410
of the concepts in this movie and why the
characters did what they did.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:32.029
But keep it down.

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:33.970
They are listening.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:37.440
The beginning of the film offers a lot of
clues as to how the creatures' takeover went

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:38.440
down.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.860
We see the Abbott family wander into an abandoned
town.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.900
Yes, their last name is Abbott, it's only
ever shown on their mailbox and in the credits.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:47.000
This is 89 days into the takeover.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.370
The town is abandoned, but not completely
destroyed.

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:53.180
There's a board filled with missing posters,
something you've seen a lot of if you watch

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:54.670
Things You Missed regularly.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:58.660
But this is our first clue, it tells us that
the takeover happened gradually.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:03.260
It wasn't a massive attack on mankind, it
just started as a couple missing people.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:07.050
There isn't really a lot of damage to the
town, but we do see a stoplight overturned,

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:08.650
which could also be a hint.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:12.370
Later on in the movie, we see the mom go into
the basement and turn the string lights from

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:13.930
yellow to red.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:17.550
The red lights emit a small high pitched sound,
which seems to drive the creatures crazy or

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.540
at least distract them in some way.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:23.820
So likely what happened here is the creatures
struck down this light out of anger or confusion

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:28.110
which happens to be a hint towards what their
ultimate weakness is at the end of the movie.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:31.619
So then I found myself asking: How bad is
this apocalypse though?

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:33.140
How many survivors are there?

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:37.260
The plot doesn't give us a direct answer,
but I was able to scrape together some evidence.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:40.350
And as a quick side note, that's one of the
things I liked about the movie.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:44.640
I was thinking recently about The Metroid
Prime Trilogy, and how unique the storytelling

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:48.320
is with how there aren't really any scenes
in the games for the most part, but there

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:52.540
is still really detailed world building and
backstory if you explore all of the world

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:56.570
by examining things, reading journals and
drawing your own conclusions.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:00.420
I've come to call this technique "indirect
storytelling", but I had also come to the

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.950
conclusion that it wouldn't really work for
a movie.

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:05.270
But I think A Quiet Place kind of pulls it
off.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:08.590
So, back to the question: who are the survivors.

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:11.939
In the first scene where the Dad lights the
fire on top of the corn silo, we can see a

00:02:11.939 --> 00:02:16.319
couple of other fires in the distance, which
tells me that there are other survivors nearby,

00:02:16.319 --> 00:02:18.349
but they are few and far between.

00:02:18.349 --> 00:02:22.220
One of those survivors could be the old man
that the father and son encounter in the woods,

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:26.379
but I guess he loses hope when the monsters
get to his wife and he kills himself by screaming

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:28.329
out and letting them get him.

00:02:28.329 --> 00:02:31.849
So the number of families near the Abbotts
is dwindling, and it's probably good that

00:02:31.849 --> 00:02:34.549
they don't live near each other anyways for
safeties sake.

00:02:34.549 --> 00:02:37.249
But I think there are survivors in other places.

00:02:37.249 --> 00:02:40.469
The most interesting one to me, comes from
a newspaper headline pinned to the wall in

00:02:40.469 --> 00:02:43.090
the basement which reads "go underground".

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:46.599
Later in the movie, we essentially see that
going underground to isolate any noise you

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:49.799
might make seems to work pretty well, because
they are able to speak to each other in the

00:02:49.799 --> 00:02:51.439
underground nursery.

00:02:51.439 --> 00:02:55.449
That's why I'm making this video down here.

00:02:55.449 --> 00:02:59.010
I'd be interested to see this world through,
from the perspective of someone who successfully

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.689
hid out underground.

00:03:00.689 --> 00:03:04.939
There could even be a whole underground city
for all we know, but if it gets too big, it

00:03:04.939 --> 00:03:05.939
could mean trouble.

00:03:05.939 --> 00:03:09.569
Leave a like on this video if that's a movie
you'd like to see in the future.

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:13.650
More evidence we have of other survivors is
shown in a scene where the Dad uses his broadcast

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.999
equipment to reach out to other countries.

00:03:15.999 --> 00:03:19.849
We see him cross countries off of a long list,
and it doesn't look like he ever made contact

00:03:19.849 --> 00:03:20.849
with any of them.

00:03:20.849 --> 00:03:24.849
But that don't mean there aren't other survivors
out there, I think there are just other families

00:03:24.849 --> 00:03:29.180
like the Abbotts, but they probably don't
have access to broadcast equipment.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:32.340
And the last evidence of other survivors is
that the power still works.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:35.419
They have electricity, so there's got to be
someone out there running a power plant of

00:03:35.419 --> 00:03:36.419
some kind.

00:03:36.419 --> 00:03:40.170
A generator wouldn't work because it would
make too much noise.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:43.260
And while we're on the topic of what they
do to keep the noise level, I thought I'd

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:46.080
explain some of the ones you might not have
picked up on.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.510
Some of these might be obvious but I think
you'll learn a few things.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:52.799
The best thing you can do to reduce unwanted
sound is to soften the point of impact, which

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:56.609
slows down the impact and reduces both volume
and reverberation.

00:03:56.609 --> 00:04:01.379
If you knock on a hard object it's obviously
going to louder than if you knock on a soft

00:04:01.379 --> 00:04:02.379
object.

00:04:02.379 --> 00:04:04.290
Sounds waves work the same way.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:08.849
So when I record these video I use these foam
sound panels to try to deaden the sound.

00:04:08.849 --> 00:04:11.969
The Abbotts take this concept and apply it
wherever they can.

00:04:11.969 --> 00:04:14.489
They paste old newspapers up all around the
nursery.

00:04:14.489 --> 00:04:16.829
They put empty egg cartons on the furniture.

00:04:16.829 --> 00:04:20.979
Not only are they soft, but the irregular
angles bounce sounds waves in random directions

00:04:20.979 --> 00:04:22.650
to help reduce echo.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:27.009
The mobile above the baby's bed has plush
swans which should also help prevent the baby

00:04:27.009 --> 00:04:28.009
from crying.

00:04:28.009 --> 00:04:30.699
I mean, theoretically of course.

00:04:30.699 --> 00:04:32.880
The Monopoly pieces they use are soft shapes.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:36.070
The dice appear to be hard, which is why they
roll them on a blanket.

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:40.479
The daughter's room is filled with stuffed
dog, pillows and just anything to dampen the

00:04:40.479 --> 00:04:41.479
sound.

00:04:41.479 --> 00:04:44.430
Obviously they can't use a laundry machine,
but having a clothesline in front of the house

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:48.370
that is always loaded up with clothing is
a great idea, especially considering how much

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:52.449
of a big wide open area they live in, it could
be very helpful to dull some of the sounds

00:04:52.449 --> 00:04:54.979
that escape the house and keep them from getting
too far.

00:04:54.979 --> 00:04:57.360
You probably noticed that they never wear
shoes.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:01.139
And a mattress is a perfect door to the bunker
because it's literally the most soundproof

00:05:01.139 --> 00:05:02.280
thing they have.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:04.479
I could go on and on but I think you get the
point.

00:05:04.479 --> 00:05:08.840
There were only a couple questions I had about
their practices, so let's open up a discussion

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:10.379
in the comments.

00:05:10.379 --> 00:05:11.740
Quietly.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:15.710
First thing was I noticed they have a refrigerator,
which makes noise when plugged in.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:19.539
I'm guessing they just have it off all the
time and maybe use it as a cooler just to

00:05:19.539 --> 00:05:21.939
slow down the time it takes food to get warm.

00:05:21.939 --> 00:05:24.590
My other question was about the fire he starts
each night.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.870
I would think the crackle of the fire would
be loud enough to attract those creatures.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:31.130
Next I'm going to talk about the origins of
these creatures.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.610
I'll be looking to answer a few questions
like:

00:05:33.610 --> 00:05:34.840
Where do they come from?

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:36.289
How many are there?

00:05:36.289 --> 00:05:37.389
When does this movie takes place?

00:05:37.389 --> 00:05:40.129
How is are the Abbotts able to beat them?

00:05:40.129 --> 00:05:41.879
And why do they kill?

00:05:41.879 --> 00:05:46.169
Based on the evidence I saw in the movie,
I think these creatures are aliens.

00:05:46.169 --> 00:05:48.409
Remember how I said the takeover wasn't immediate?

00:05:48.409 --> 00:05:53.520
I think these aliens came to earth in a small
group and gradually reproduced to cover the

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:54.520
globe.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:58.090
Sound would not be an issue for them in outer
space because sound can't travel in space,

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:01.810
and their home planet probably has very little
atmosphere for sound to travel upon as well.

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:05.830
There are also numerous references to space
left by the film's art department.

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:09.689
The original toy that sets off the first killing
is a rocket ship.

00:06:09.689 --> 00:06:13.490
The son's pillowcase and window have stars
on them and newspaper headlines refer to the

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:16.259
National Guard declaring a state of emergency.

00:06:16.259 --> 00:06:19.659
And the Monopoly pieces used resemble a star
and planet.

00:06:19.659 --> 00:06:22.020
So how many aliens are there?

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:24.050
Like I said, they multiply.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:26.909
But the Dad identifies that he thinks there
are 3 in the area.

00:06:26.909 --> 00:06:32.240
At the end, we see more than that, but I think
there are actually many many more than that.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:33.970
We saw how fast these things can move.

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:35.190
And it's pretty fast.

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:38.509
But it never takes more than a few seconds
for one to strike after a noise.

00:06:38.509 --> 00:06:41.729
There's also a night scene early on in the
movie where you can hear their cries in the

00:06:41.729 --> 00:06:46.080
distance and it seems like there are way,
way more in the area.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:47.729
When does the movie take place?

00:06:47.729 --> 00:06:50.070
We can actually determine that pretty accurately.

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:52.680
The movie starts on Day 89 of the invasion.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.479
That's the day the four-year-old dies.

00:06:54.479 --> 00:06:57.630
His memorial reads 2016-2020.

00:06:57.630 --> 00:07:03.020
Just over 1 year later, on Day 473, we see
a calendar dated Oct 3rd, and that's most

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:06.460
likely 2021, and that's where the rest of
the movie takes place.

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:09.389
The weekdays don't seem to line up with our
real world calendar though.

00:07:09.389 --> 00:07:13.639
I know a lot of people are going to ask why
the daughter's hearing aid hurt the aliens.

00:07:13.639 --> 00:07:17.629
Despite these aliens having incredibly sensitive
eardrums, we can assume their hearing works

00:07:17.629 --> 00:07:18.960
on the same principles.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:21.740
Like humans, they have a range of frequencies
that they can hear.

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:24.860
The hearing aid just takes certain frequencies
and amplifies them.

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:30.409
However, the aliens' enourmous ears, like
any microphone, are generating some self noise.

00:07:30.409 --> 00:07:33.430
So the hearing aid is picking up those frequencies
and making them louder.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:38.860
Then the aliens ears are taking THOSE amplified
sounds and emitting more self noise.

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:40.680
The result is a feedback loop.

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:44.860
If you've ever been in a video chat without
headphones, you've probably experienced this.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:46.330
It's not a pleasant sound.

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:50.270
However, I'm guessing that the sound being
amplified is mostly outside the human range

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:51.270
of hearing.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:56.490
But if the aliens have a wider range of hearing,
much like dogs do, the feedback loop probably

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:58.809
drives them crazy and hurts them.

00:07:58.809 --> 00:08:01.599
That kind of leads into why these aliens kill.

00:08:01.599 --> 00:08:05.580
There's no evidence anywhere of them eating
their victims or collecting food.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:10.029
They probably just kill because the sounds
we make are extremely annoying to them.

00:08:10.029 --> 00:08:12.939
Much like how I may one day kill West Dakota.

00:08:12.939 --> 00:08:17.080
But that will have to be another day, because
today I just have to keep quiet from these

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:18.080
aliens.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.900
If you're looking for some more great horror,
you should check out these island horror stories

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:21.900
I wrote.

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:26.539
Barely anyone saw this video and I honestly
think it's the best video I've ever written.

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:30.020
The great part is you can just throw in some
headphones and listen to these scary stories,

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:32.919
and you shouldn't have to worry about the
aliens coming after you.

